@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      INTENDED -- responsibility and data flow, as the authority
'           documents describe it.
' GROUNDING PRODUCT.md ("The intended journey", "Existing pieces",
'           "What is live code vs research record"); README.md
'           ("What is implemented now", "Repository map").
'
' THE ARROWS HERE ARE NOT IMPORT EDGES. They say which component is
' responsible for handing what to which, not which module imports which.
' For the measured dependency structure see 05-package-dependencies.puml,
' which disagrees with this view on purpose -- see ADR-0002 and
' docs/development/discrepancy-register.md D4.
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — live responsibilities and data flow (INTENDED)

package "Input + observation" {
  component "adapters" as Adapters
  component "inspector" as Inspector
}

package "Definition" {
  component "modeller" as Modeller
  component "taskmodel" as TaskModel
}

package "Task families" {
  component "reservation" as Reservation
  component "enrichment" as Enrichment
  component "aggregation" as Aggregation
  component "reconciliation" as Reconciliation
}

package "Deterministic operation" {
  component "worker" as Worker
  component "fleet" as Fleet
  component "calendar_job" as CalendarJob
}

package "Interpretation + improvement" {
  component "supervisor" as Supervisor
}

Adapters --> Inspector : structural data
Inspector --> Modeller : observed facts / evidence
Modeller --> TaskModel : explicit task model
TaskModel --> Reservation
TaskModel --> Enrichment
TaskModel --> Aggregation
TaskModel --> Reconciliation
Reservation --> Worker
Enrichment --> Worker
Aggregation --> Worker
Reconciliation --> Worker
Worker --> Fleet : established worker state / runs
CalendarJob --> Worker : unattended reservation path
Fleet --> Supervisor : fleet context / exceptions / map state
Supervisor ..> Fleet : investigation / improvement proposals

note right of Modeller
Current DEFINE surface.
Large pipeline remains live product code.
end note

note right of Fleet
Owns established fleet/operations and
derives the read-only system map from
authority-bearing state.
end note

note right of Supervisor
May interpret, investigate and propose.
Does not silently establish, promote or
execute authority-bearing changes.
end note

note bottom
**Flow, not dependency.** Of the fifteen arrows here, only two
(modeller/taskmodel, supervisor/fleet) also run in the direction the
code depends. Eight run the opposite way to the real import, and five
describe a hand-off that no import performs at all -- including
adapters/inspector and calendar_job/worker. Thirteen further real
dependencies are deliberately absent, because they are not steps in
the flow.

That is correct for a flow view and wrong for a dependency one, which
is why these are two files. See 05-package-dependencies.puml.
end note
@enduml
